Ordered value constraints
-------------------------

* Ready-made LessThanConstraint, LessThanOrEqualConstraint,
  GreaterThanConstraint and GreaterThanOrEqualConstraint own comparison bounds
  and generate usage/error text through the predicate core.
* Inclusive RangeConstraint remains available with unchanged boundary behavior.
* Ordered comparisons reject NaN values/bounds and avoid bound arithmetic.

Callable constraints
--------------------

* PredicateConstraint adapts owned functions and function objects; independent
  description and short ID strings supply error and usage text.
* MakeRuleConstraint shares rule state with computed descriptions and short IDs.
* C++20 MakeConstraint supports capturing lambdas, move-only callable
  state and const invocation. Empty callable objects fail at construction.
